Error: Jet.UseWhileWriteActive: `tally` is changed by a stored lambda that holds its own copy, so it can't be used here
  --> Tests/UI/stored_closure_capture_write_field_read.jet:18:11
    |
 18 |     print(tally.count)
    |           ^^^^^^^^^^^
 Why: A stored lambda owns its captures: its writes land on its copy of `tally` and never reach `tally` itself
 Fix: Call the lambda only where it is bound so it borrows `tally`, or keep the value in a `Shared` or `Cell` the lambda and this code both reach
More: jet-lang.dev/e/Jet.UseWhileWriteActive
